## **The Two Main Pages**

### **PAGE 1: index.html (Upload Page)**

**What it shows:**
1. Hero section with title
2. Three feature cards (what the app does)
3. Upload form for JD and Resume
4. Submit button

**Let's break it down:**

```html
<!-- HEADER/HERO SECTION -->
<div class="hero-section">
    <h1>AI Skill Assessment Agent</h1>
    <p>Analyze job descriptions and resumes...</p>
</div>
```

**Styled with CSS:**
```css
.hero-section {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);
    /* Purple gradient background */
    color: white;
    padding: 3rem 0;
}
```

**Result:** Purple gradient header with white text

---

**Feature Cards:**
```html
<div class="col-md-4">
    <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">
            <i class="fas fa-search"></i>
        </div>
        <h5>Skill Analysis</h5>
        <p>Extract and analyze skills...</p>
    </div>
</div>
```

**What happens:**
- `col-md-4` = Takes 1/3 of the width (Bootstrap grid)
- `fas fa-search` = Icon from Font Awesome (a library of icons)
- Three of these side-by-side show three features

**Result:** Three nice cards with icons

---

**Upload Form:**
```html
<form action="/assess" method="post" enctype="multipart/form-data">
    <!-- This sends data to app.py when clicked -->
    
    <input type="file" name="jd_file" accept=".txt,.pdf,.doc,.docx">
    <!-- File upload input -->
    
    <textarea name="jd_text" placeholder="Paste the job description here...">
    <!-- Text area for pasting text -->
    
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">
        Generate Assessment
    </button>
</form>
```

**How it works:**
1. User uploads a file OR pastes text
2. Clicks "Generate Assessment"
3. Form sends data to Flask: `action="/assess"`
4. Flask processes it (the Python backend)
5. Redirects to results page

**Like:** Filling out a form and submitting it

---

**JavaScript (Interactive):**
```javascript
// File input styling
document.getElementById('jd_file').addEventListener('change', function(e) {
    if (e.target.files.length > 0) {
        document.getElementById('jd_text').value = '';
        // If user uploads file, clear the text box
    }
});
```

**What happens:**
- When user uploads a file, the textarea is automatically cleared
- Prevents confusion (file OR text, not both)

